A direct remote identification add-on must broadcast the following data in real time during the entire duration of the flight, using an open and documented transmission protocol that can be received by existing mobile devices [Reg 2019/945, PART 6 Requirements for a direct remote identification add-on]:

*   The UAS operator registration number and the verification code provided by the Member State of registration (unless the consistency check is not passed) [Reg 2019/945, PART 6 Requirements for a direct remote identification add-on];
*   The unique serial number of the add-on [Reg 2019/945, PART 6 Requirements for a direct remote identification add-on];
*   The time stamp, the geographical position of the UA, and its height above the surface or take-off point [Reg 2019/945, PART 6 Requirements for a direct remote identification add-on];
*   The route course (measured clockwise from true north) and the ground speed of the UA [Reg 2019/945, PART 6 Requirements for a direct remote identification add-on];
*   The geographical position of the remote pilot or, if not available, the take-off point [Reg 2019/945, PART 6 Requirements for a direct remote identification add-on].

This information is based on the 2020 consolidated version of Regulation 2019/945.
